# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and environment-specific configuration
#
# Database credentials live ONLY on the host, in an ACL-protected location
# outside the repository (spec section 9, gap G-10). Nothing here should ever
# need un-ignoring - if you are tempted, you are about to commit a credential.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
appsettings.Production.json
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.Local.json
secrets.json
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
connectionstrings.json

# Backups and database dumps - these contain live operational data
backups/
*.sql.gz
*.dump
!db/migrations/*.sql

# Local logs
logs/
*.log
!evidence/**/*.log

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Local scratch
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code
#
# .claude/settings.json IS committed - the guardrail hooks must apply to
# everyone working in this repo. Only machine-specific overrides belong in
# settings.local.json, and those stay local. If you are tempted to move a
# guardrail into the local file to stop it complaining, the guardrail is
# telling you something real.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json

# Fleet worker run logs - transcripts and raw JSON, never committed.
# The registry, briefs, and mission ledger ARE committed; only the run output is noise.
.claude/fleet/runs/

# Health check results. Same reasoning: the checklist and the script are committed, a
# particular run's verdict is a local observation about one machine at one moment.
.claude/fleet/health/
